      <h1>DataFrames and Basic <span class="accent">Operations</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Master Pandas DataFrames—the fundamental data structure for data science. Learn to create DataFrames from various sources, inspect data structure and content, and perform essential operations that form the foundation of all data analysis workflows. DataFrames are where your data analysis journey begins, combining the power of labeled columns with flexible operations.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="objectives">
      <h4>Learning Objectives</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Understand the DataFrame structure and how it differs from NumPy arrays and Python dictionaries</li>
        <li>Create DataFrames from dictionaries, lists, arrays, and other data sources with appropriate parameters</li>
        <li>Navigate the anatomy of a DataFrame: index, columns, values, and dtypes with proper interpretation</li>
        <li>Perform basic operations: selection, arithmetic, and string methods on columns and rows</li>
